A||||15||86 SE||changing speakers||||6||
Z||000000||86 SE||05-12-2000||05:31 PM||||Im going to put a new set of factory speakers in my 86 SE & I was wondering if you guys had any tips on how to do it <BR>         Tanks guys||||reg||6
Z||000001||86 SE||05-12-2000||05:33 PM||||one thing I forgot its in the back of the car||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||05-12-2000||05:41 PM||||DO NOT try to just pop the speaker cover off. You need to remove the whole panel. You will need a rather large torx bit to remove the seat belt attachment. Otherwise I don't remember anything unusual. Just be careful with that big plastic panel and don't rip the headliner or anything like that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||05-12-2000||07:29 PM||||What DRH said! Don't force anything, that's the key. Take the upper seat belt anchor out first. Seems like I only remember a few screws, then just turn it the right way to get the whole inner sail panel out. There's a slit in the panel where the seat belt slides through too. Not to hard, really.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-12-2000||10:14 PM||||My '86 had some small clips holding the seatbelt slots together ('85 did not).  Watch out for those.  I think there's a screw on the leading edge of the sail panel, too.  The back is held on with a tar-like substance.  It'll come off, but have patience.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homicidal||05-13-2000||03:21 AM||||What are you guys talking about?  Did Pontiac put more speakers into the 86 models?<P>My 84 on has two speakers in the dash and two in the headrest!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||05-13-2000||03:37 AM||||In 86 pontiac got rid of the headrest speakers and put 4x6's in the sail panels.<BR>  <BR>The seatbelt anchor bolt is a t-50 torx bit, same as the brake caliper bolts.  There is one other screw in the leading edge, in the middle of the door frame.  After you have those out it's just a little wiggling and pulling and it's out.  3 screws hold the speaker in, and you'll probably have to reuse the plastic surround that holds the speaker in.  you'll know when you see it.<P><I>"Installation is reverse of removal"</I>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Homicidal||05-13-2000||03:51 AM||||That sux @ss!<P>I wonder if I could mount some 4X6's on there, might be able to....<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ounmongk||05-13-2000||11:52 AM||||in the case of the 4x6's: would you want to upgrade them to a better set than factory? those speakers (IMO) can't really take that much power. I just upgraded the front speakers and turn the fader to the front, my rear speakers suck. (factory) keep us posted, 86... anyone upgraded the 4x6's? does it sound any better than factory? not too sure about how much these little things can take, but anything's possible nowadays.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||05-13-2000||12:38 PM||||I have a set of 4x6s for sale.  Brand new Kenwoods (4x10s for sale, too).  Email me if anyone is interested.||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||05-13-2000||04:36 PM||||The factory 4" X 6" speakers are wimpy, but aftermarket ones, like the Kenwood's, Pioneer's, etc. kick butt and sound great.||||reg||1
Z||000011||86 SE||05-13-2000||05:24 PM||||wich ones should i get i want to keep it organal||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||05-13-2000||07:52 PM||||The correct sized aftermarket speakers are a direct bolt in. You do have to splice in the correct wire terminals or use an adapter plug. But, once the covers are on, nobody can tell they're not original. If you truly want factory originals, then you'll have to buy them from the GM dealership, but they won't sound nearly as good as say, Monkey's new Kenwood speakers that he'd sell you for a good price.||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||05-13-2000||09:07 PM||||Even my cheapy Jensen coaxials that I paid &lt;$40 sound much mo better the factory. It's worth it!||||reg||1
Z||000014||86 SE||05-14-2000||12:47 AM||||sume day i will want the factory ones back in it will i be able to do that||||reg||1
Z||000015||batboy||05-14-2000||01:56 AM||||Yes, if you use the wire adapters instead of cutting the speaker wires and splicing new terminals on. I saved the factory speakers out of my 87 SE for that same reason.||||reg||1
